+- Keep chat functionality unchanged
+- Store memory in markdown files
+- Separate Memory Engine from chat flow
+- Use dedicated memory folders
+
+==================================================
+INVALID DECISION EXAMPLES
+==================================================
+
+Examples:
+
+- Generic technical facts
+- AI-generated assumptions
+- Unaccepted recommendations
+- Future possibilities
+- Speculation
+- Implementation ideas that were never agreed upon
+
+==================================================
+PROJECT SAFETY RULES
+==================================================
+
+Keep existing functionality unchanged.
+
+Do NOT modify:
+
+- frontend
+- chat API structure
+- RAW storage
+- existing Ollama chat flow
+
+Do NOT replace working functionality.
+
+Only extend the Memory Engine.
+
+==================================================
+IMPLEMENTATION REVIEW
+==================================================
+
+Before writing code:
+
+1. Review the architecture.
+2. Identify design flaws.
+3. Identify memory duplication risks.
+4. Identify decision tracking risks.
+5. Identify future scaling risks.
+
+Then improve the implementation if needed.
+
+==================================================
+SUCCESS CRITERIA
+==================================================
+
+Conversation
+→ RAW
+→ Summary
+→ Decisions
+→ Markdown files
+
+Requirements:
+
